    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d362">

                <pb facs="0616" n="602" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg602"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 European War 1939/2559: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Hamilton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-05-01T22:00:00+03:00">May 1, 1944—10
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received May 2—1:12 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1535. See my 1514, April 29, 11 p.m. It seems likely that the inquiry made of me
                    at the Foreign Office on April 29 may have been related to the question of the
                    inclusion in Stalin’s May 1 order of the day of the warning to Rumania, Hungary,
                    Finland and Bulgaria to get out of the war.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hamilton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
